# Project-Specific Guidelines

What every change to nbkp must respect beyond the shared
[iglootools guidelines](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/README.md): where
the conventions for particular areas live, which shared rules do not apply, where nbkp departs
from them, the rules it adds, the patches its tests make, and which documents each kind of change
updates. Read it before any change; it overrides the shared guidelines as
[applying-the-guidelines.md › Precedence](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/applying-the-guidelines.md#precedence)
describes.

## Area conventions

Read the linked document in full before changing files under these paths.

| Paths | Conventions |
|-------|-------------|
| `nbkp/cli/`, `nbkp/*/cli/` — and adding a command or option anywhere | [cli.md](guidelines/cli.md) — the helper modules, and the exceptions to the shared CLI rules |
| `tests/`, `nbkp/*/testkit/` | [testing.md](guidelines/testing.md) — which suite a test goes in, and the deciders, fakes and resources to test with |

## Out of scope

| Shared section | Why it does not apply |
|---|---|
| [cli-demo.md](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/project-setup/cli-demo.md) | <the reason, such as: the project ships no CLI> |

## Exceptions

### Keep the SSH timeout keys in plain seconds

Overrides [general.md › Name from the domain's vocabulary, then the surface's conventions](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/coding/general.md#name-from-the-domains-vocabulary-then-the-surfaces-conventions):
`connect-timeout` and the other SSH timeout keys are numbers of seconds, with no unit in the name.

**Why:** they are configuration keys users have written, and they mirror the OpenSSH option names
they map to.

**Retires when:** a major release accepts durations with a unit (`10s`), keeping a bare number as
seconds.

## Rules

### Mirror a change to `run` or the sync logic in `sh`

A change to the `run` command or to `nbkp/sync/` is mirrored in the script `sh` generates, or the
code says why `sh` drops it.

**Why:** `sh` is the same backup as a standalone script, and a difference nobody wrote down reads as
a bug in one of them.

## Tests

Tests patch only in the cases
[general.md › Patch only in the three documented cases](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/coding/general.md#patch-only-in-the-three-documented-cases-and-list-each-one)
allows, enforced as
[python-tooling.md › Enforce the patching rule](https://github.com/iglootools/common/blob/main/guidelines/project-setup/python-tooling.md#enforce-the-patching-rule)
sets up. Each patch nbkp has:

| File | What it replaces | Category | Why | Retires when |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `tests/remote/test_docker_testkit.py` | `docker.from_env` | (a) | checks the port binding handed to the Docker SDK without a Docker daemon | the container starters take the client as a parameter |

## Documentation

| A change to | Updates |
|---|---|
| a command or option | `docs/cli-reference.md` (`mise run clidocs`), `features.md`, `usage.md` |
| a config field | `docs/config-reference.md` (`mise run configdocs`, then the prose the generator cannot derive), `usage.md` |
| an entity or an invariant | `domain.md` |
| a module or the layering | `architecture.md` and the import-linter contracts; `mise run depgraph` |
| a patch in a test | the [table above](#tests) |
